{"name":"Placebo Sky","hex":"#ebfcfc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"placebo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dummy medicine containing no active ingredients; an inert treatment. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The vespers sung in the office for the dead."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/placebo"},{"term":"sky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Sikaiana."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The atmosphere above a given point, especially as visible from the surface of the Earth as the place where the sun, moon, stars, and clouds are seen.","With a descriptive word: the part of the sky which can be seen from a specific place or at a specific time; its climate, condition, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sky"}],"entries":[{"title":"Placebo","blocks":[{"text":"A placebo is a medicine or treatment intended to appear genuine to its recipient, but which has no pharmaceutical effect. Common placebos include inert tablets, inert injections, sham surgery, and other procedures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Cebocap.jpg/330px-Cebocap.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Placebo","wikidata":"Q269829"},{"title":"Sky","blocks":[{"text":"The sky is an unobstructed view upward from the surface of the Earth. It includes the atmosphere and outer space. It may also be considered a place between the ground and outer space, thus distinct from outer space."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg/330px-July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky","wikidata":"Q527"},{"title":"Sky blue","blocks":[{"text":"Sky blue refers to a collection of shades comparable to that of a clear daytime sky. Typically it is a shade of cyan or light teal, though some iterations are closer to light azure or light blue. The term is attested from 1681. A 1585 translation of Nicolas de Nicolay's 1576 Les navigations, peregrinations et voyages faicts en la Turquie includes \"the tulbant [turban] of the merchant must be skie coloured\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Shades_of_light_blue.png/330px-Shades_of_light_blue.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky_blue","wikidata":"Q373160"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/%22Miracle_Cure%21%22_Health_Fraud_Scams_%288528312890%29.jpg/500px-%22Miracle_Cure%21%22_Health_Fraud_Scams_%288528312890%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/%22Miracle_Cure%21%22_Health_Fraud_Scams_%288528312890%29.jpg/1280px-%22Miracle_Cure%21%22_Health_Fraud_Scams_%288528312890%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/%22Miracle_Cure%21%22_Health_Fraud_Scams_%288528312890%29.jpg/500px-%22Miracle_Cure%21%22_Health_Fraud_Scams_%288528312890%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The subjective effects of placebos may be related to expectations, yet similar effects have been noted in open-label studies.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%22Miracle_Cure!%22_Health_Fraud_Scams_(8528312890).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/James_Gillray%2C_%22Metallic_Tractors%22%2C_showing_Elisha_Perkins_Wellcome_M0010466.jpg/500px-James_Gillray%2C_%22Metallic_Tractors%22%2C_showing_Elisha_Perkins_Wellcome_M0010466.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org